From 9e3fd84d30d18ea8e4420b3a49b986ccd3e5c2e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] v2: swap tagged hashes and commitments from CSHA256 to BLAKE3

Switch Lotus V2 domain-separated tagged hashes and Merklix commitments
from CSHA256 to hardware-accelerated BLAKE3.

Original-Commit: 5e71940ab2c3991d9ca9c3424dd698917a295db5
Original-Patch: v2/006
Split-Concern: whole

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.

Candidate-Application-Repair: Apply required V2 BLAKE3 tagged hashing while retaining the shared PreconsensusBatch domain. Remove obsolete SHA256 midstate helpers only at this explicit V2 boundary; eCash prefix continues using SHA256 as validated.

Stack-Repair-Plan-v2: Use the existing TaggedHash(HashDomain::PreconsensusBatch,serialized announcement) path; this native boundary supplies BLAKE3(domain||NUL||payload), without a second keyed-BLAKE3 scheme. Shared eCash SHA256 identifiers remain unchanged. Independent168-byte vector and actual-code before/after gate accompany this owner.

(cherry picked from commit 7e08d8568a41c8387b2d98543e979157195e3ce4)

